# This is a file of tests for the GMOS sequencer in a suitable format to be read
# by the tcsTests.tk procedure.
# 
# This particular test file is aimed at checking the input ranges to 
# the GMOS 'atmPos' CAD command.
#
#
# Comments are introduced by a # in the first column
# Blank lines can be left if required.
# The currently allowed keywords are (case is immaterial)
#
#  Test   <testId>
#  Command <commandName>
#  Field   <CAD field> <value>
#  Response Accept | Reject
#  Timeout <msecs>
#  OnError Continue | Abort
#  Log     <recordName>
#  Directive Start | Preset

# This first part before the first Test keyword can be used to setup 
# global values for Response, TimeOut and OnError. These global values
# can be over ridden within specific tests

Response Reject
TimeOut  30000
OnError  Continue

Help
Help These tests checks the trapping of invalid input to the
Help atmPos command.
Help
Help The first tests check for null input. If the commands in question have
Help been run at any time after booting and prior to running these tests then
Help there will already be input on the CAD fields and so these null tests
Help will fail. To validate the trapping of null input you will have to
Help reboot the GMOS sequencer and start these tests again.
Help
Help Press continue when ready
Help

# Tests start here. Each test must start with the Test keyword, end with
# a Directive keyword and have at least one Command keyword. Any Field
# keywords are assumed to apply to the last command

Test UT03010
Summary Check rejection of null input
Help Check rejection of null input

 Command atmPos 
 Field  DIR MARK   
 Response  Reject 
 Directive Start

Test UT03020
Summary Check rejection of null input to Exit prism angle field
Help Check rejection of null input to Exit prism angle field 

 Command atmPos 
 Field  A  40.0
 Response  Reject 
 Directive Start

Test UT03030
Summary Check rejection of invalid input to Entrance prism angle field
Help Check rejection of invalid input to Entrance prism angle field

 Command atmPos 
 Field  A  XXXXX 
 Field  B  40.0
 Response  Reject 
 Directive Start

Test UT03040
Summary Check rejection of invalid input to Exit prism angle field
Help Check rejection of invalid input to Exit prism angle field

 Command atmPos 
 Field  A  40.0 
 Field  B  XXXXX
 Response  Reject 
 Directive Start

Test UT03050
Summary Check rejection of out-of-range (positive) input to Entrance prism angle field
Help Check rejection of out-of-range (positive) input to Entrance prism angle field

 Command atmPos 
 Field  A  9999.0
 Field  B  40.0
 Response  Reject 
 Directive Start

Test UT03060
Summary Check rejection of out-of-range (negative) input to Entrance prism angle field
Help Check rejection of out-of-range (negative) input to Entrance prism angle field

 Command atmPos 
 Field  A  -9999.0
 Field  B  40.0
 Response  Reject 
 Directive Start

Test UT03070
Summary Check rejection of out-of-range (positive) input to Exit prism angle field
Help Check rejection of out-of-range (positive) input to Exit prism angle field

 Command atmPos 
 Field  A  40.0
 Field  B  9999.0
 Response  Reject 
 Directive Start

Test UT03080
Summary Check rejection of out-of-range (negative) input to Exit prism angle field
Help Check rejection of out-of-range (negative) input to Exit prism angle field

 Command atmPos 
 Field  A  40.0
 Field  B  -9999.0
 Response  Reject 
 Directive Start

Test UT03090
Summary Check rejection of out-of-range input to both fields
Help Check rejection of out-of-range input to both fields

 Command atmPos 
 Field  A  9999.0
 Field  B  -9999.0
 Response  Reject 
 Directive Start


Test UT03100
Summary Check acceptance of valid Entrance and Exit prism angle fields
Help Check acceptance of valid Entrance and Exit prism angle fields

  Aftertest Pause

 Command atmPos 
  Field  A  45.0
  Field  B  45.0
  Response  Accept
  Directive Start

# Test UT03110
# Summary Check that rejection by Components Controller is reported correctly
# NO TEST AVAILABLE
#
